# Git Commit Title Guideline

Apply this rule when the user asks to create a git commit or push commits.

## Title Format

- Write the title in English only.
- Keep the title within 50 characters.
- Start with one verb: Add / Update / Remove / Improve / Refactor.
- Do not end the title with a period.
- Avoid vague titles. Do not use standalone words like "update", "work", or "test".

## Type Prefix

Use exactly one prefix at the start of the title:

- `#feat`: Add a new feature.
- `#fix`: Fix a bug.
- `#asset`: Add or update assets (sprite, sound, animation, etc.).
- `#scene`: Change scene files.
- `#refactor`: Refactor code without behavior change.
- `#perf`: Improve performance.
- `#docs`: Update documentation.
- `#chore`: Build config, Unity version, or package changes.
- `#revert`: Revert a previous commit.

## Valid Example

`#feat Add combo damage scaling by weapon tier`
